IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Commonwealth of Australia Constitution Act 1900 (Imp) -- covering clause 9, the Constitution: who is capable of being
-- chosen as a senator or a member of the House of Representatives. Sections 16 and 34 (qualifications), 43 (a member of one
-- House cannot be chosen for the other), 44 (disqualification: (i) foreign allegiance or citizenship, (ii) treason and
-- conviction, (iii) bankruptcy, (iv) office of profit and pension under the Crown, (v) interest in an agreement with the Public
-- Service of the Commonwealth, and the proviso to (iv)), 45 (what vacates the place once chosen) and 46 (the penalty for
-- sitting while incapable).
--
-- SEAT: the would-be candidate -- the person who wants to stand for the Senate or the House of Representatives (Daniel, a
-- dual Australian and Italian citizen, in 2040). Every decision is phrased as that person would ask it ("Am I incapable of
-- being chosen under section 44", "Am I capable of being chosen", "Would my place become vacant").
--
-- RENUNCIATION. Whether a person is "a subject or a citizen ... of a foreign power" is a matter of that power's law, which is
-- not in this deposit. This encoding encodes the TEXT: a person who has held a foreign citizenship is still a citizen unless
-- the renunciation HAS TAKEN EFFECT under the foreign law; that is an INPUT. The High Court's gloss -- that a person who has
-- taken all reasonable steps to renounce, but whom the foreign law makes it impossible to free, is not disqualified (Sykes v
-- Cleary; Re Canavan [2017] HCA 45) -- is case law, not text, and is NOT encoded. Nor is the case law on the moment at which
-- the disqualification is tested: the text says "incapable of being chosen" and gives no date; the facts are taken as at the
-- day the person asks about.
--
-- Edition: Commonwealth of Australia Constitution Act (The Constitution), Compilation No. 6, compilation date 29 July 1977,
-- includes amendments up to Act No. 84, 1977 (register id C2013Q00005, registered 18 November 2021), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004Q00685.txt. No regulation sets a number or date for these sections.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the qualifications the Parliament has provided in place of s 34 ("Until the Parliament otherwise provides") --
-- they are in the Commonwealth Electoral Act 1918 s 163 and are asked here as a fact (see that Act's baseline encoding); the
-- oath (s 42); disputed elections and who decides (s 47 -- the House, until the Parliament otherwise provides); vacancy by
-- resignation or absence (ss 19, 20, 37, 38); everything outside Chapter I Part IV that does not bear on being chosen. Whether
-- the Parliament has "otherwise provided" for s 46 is not in this deposit, so s 46 is encoded as written.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `The Constitution -- being chosen for the Parliament`

-- The House the person seeks to be chosen for.
DECLARE `House` IS ONE OF `the Senate`, `the House of Representatives`

-- Whether the person already sits in either House (s 43).
DECLARE `My seat now` IS ONE OF
    `I sit in neither House`
    `I am a senator`
    `I am a member of the House of Representatives`

-- s 44(iv) and its proviso. "Office of profit under the Crown" is not defined in the Constitution: it is a borrowed term,
-- and which office (if any) the person holds is asked. The proviso's offices are listed so that they can be answered.
DECLARE `My office under the Crown` IS ONE OF
    `no office of profit under the Crown`
    `the office of a Minister of State of the Queen for the Commonwealth or for a State`
    `pay as an officer or member of the Commonwealth naval or military forces, my services not wholly employed by the Commonwealth`
    `pay as an officer or member of the Commonwealth naval or military forces, my services wholly employed by the Commonwealth`
    `pay or half-pay as an officer or member of the navy or army of the Queen`
    `another office of profit under the Crown`

-- The facts the would-be candidate can state. Borrowed terms (subject or citizen of a foreign power, undischarged bankrupt,
-- office of profit, subject of the Queen, elector) are asked, never worked out.
DECLARE `My circumstances` HAS
    `my date of birth` IS A DATE
    `I am an elector entitled to vote at elections of members of the House of Representatives, or qualified to become one` IS A BOOLEAN
    `years I have been resident within the Commonwealth when I am chosen` IS A NUMBER
    `I am a natural-born subject of the Queen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `years I have been naturalized under a law of the United Kingdom, a State or colony, or the Commonwealth` IS A NUMBER
    `my seat now` IS A `My seat now`
    `I am under an acknowledgment of allegiance, obedience or adherence to a foreign power` IS A BOOLEAN
    `by the law of a foreign power I have been its subject or citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my renunciation of that status has taken effect under the law of that power` IS A BOOLEAN
    `apart from citizenship, I am entitled to the rights or privileges of a subject or citizen of a foreign power` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am attainted of treason` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have been convicted of an offence and am under sentence, or subject to be sentenced, for it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the longest imprisonment that offence is punishable by under the law of the Commonwealth or a State, in months` IS A NUMBER
    `I am an undischarged bankrupt or insolvent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my office under the Crown` IS A `My office under the Crown`
    `I receive a pension payable during the pleasure of the Crown out of the revenues of the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that pension is paid to me as an officer or member of the navy or army of the Queen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have a direct or indirect pecuniary interest in an agreement with the Public Service of the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have that interest only as a member of an incorporated company, in common with its other members` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number of members of that company` IS A NUMBER

§§ `44 -- Disqualification`

-- s 44: "Any person who-- ... shall be incapable of being chosen or of sitting as a senator or a member of the House of
-- Representatives."

-- s 44(i): "Is under any acknowledgment of allegiance, obedience, or adherence to a foreign power, or is a subject or a citizen
-- or entitled to the rights or privileges of a subject or a citizen of a foreign power". The text asks whether the person
-- "is" a citizen. A foreign citizenship once held is gone only when its renunciation has taken effect under the foreign law
-- (an INPUT). Reasonable steps that the foreign law does not honour are case law, not text, and are not encoded.
@export Am I still a subject or citizen of a foreign power, by its law (s 44(i))?
GIVEN `me` IS A `My circumstances` @desc Your citizenships and any renunciation, as the foreign law treats them
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I still a citizen of a foreign power` IF
        `me`'s `by the law of a foreign power I have been its subject or citizen`
    AND (NOT `me`'s `my renunciation of that status has taken effect under the law of that power`)

@export Am I disqualified by foreign allegiance or citizenship (s 44(i))?
GIVEN `me` IS A `My circumstances` @desc Your allegiances, citizenships and any renunciation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I disqualified by foreign allegiance` IF
        `me`'s `I am under an acknowledgment of allegiance, obedience or adherence to a foreign power`
    OR  `Am I still a citizen of a foreign power` `me`
    OR  `me`'s `apart from citizenship, I am entitled to the rights or privileges of a subject or citizen of a foreign power`

-- s 44(ii): "Is attainted of treason, or has been convicted and is under sentence, or subject to be sentenced, for any offence
-- punishable under the law of the Commonwealth or of a State by imprisonment for one year or longer". The test is what the
-- offence is PUNISHABLE by, not the sentence imposed; and it lasts only while the person is under sentence or awaiting it.
@export Am I disqualified for treason or a conviction (s 44(ii))?
GIVEN `me` IS A `My circumstances` @desc Your convictions and sentences
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I disqualified by a conviction` IF
        `me`'s `I am attainted of treason`
    OR  (    `me`'s `I have been convicted of an offence and am under sentence, or subject to be sentenced, for it`
         AND `me`'s `the longest imprisonment that offence is punishable by under the law of the Commonwealth or a State, in months` AT LEAST 12)

-- s 44(iii): "Is an undischarged bankrupt or insolvent". Borrowed term, asked.
@export Am I disqualified as an undischarged bankrupt or insolvent (s 44(iii))?
GIVEN `me` IS A `My circumstances` @desc Whether you are an undischarged bankrupt or insolvent
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I disqualified as a bankrupt` IF
    `me`'s `I am an undischarged bankrupt or insolvent`

-- s 44(iv): "Holds any office of profit under the Crown, or any pension payable during the pleasure of the Crown out of any of
-- the revenues of the Commonwealth". Proviso: "sub-section iv. does not apply to the office of any of the Queen's Ministers of
-- State for the Commonwealth, or of any of the Queen's Ministers for a State, or to the receipt of pay, half-pay, or a pension
-- by any person as an officer or member of the Queen's navy or army, or to the receipt of pay as an officer or member of the
-- naval or military forces of the Commonwealth by any person whose services are not wholly employed by the Commonwealth."
GIVEN `office` IS A `My office under the Crown`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the office disqualifies` IF
    CONSIDER `office`
    WHEN `pay as an officer or member of the Commonwealth naval or military forces, my services wholly employed by the Commonwealth` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `another office of profit under the Crown` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@export Am I disqualified by an office of profit or a pension under the Crown (s 44(iv))?
GIVEN `me` IS A `My circumstances` @desc Your office or pension under the Crown, if any
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I disqualified by an office or pension` IF
        `the office disqualifies` (`me`'s `my office under the Crown`)
    OR  (    `me`'s `I receive a pension payable during the pleasure of the Crown out of the revenues of the Commonwealth`
         AND (NOT `me`'s `that pension is paid to me as an officer or member of the navy or army of the Queen`))

-- s 44(v): "Has any direct or indirect pecuniary interest in any agreement with the Public Service of the Commonwealth otherwise
-- than as a member and in common with the other members of an incorporated company consisting of more than twenty-five
-- persons". "More than twenty-five" is 26 or more.
@export Am I disqualified by an interest in an agreement with the Public Service of the Commonwealth (s 44(v))?
GIVEN `me` IS A `My circumstances` @desc Your interest in any agreement with the Commonwealth, and how you hold it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I disqualified by an interest in a Commonwealth agreement` IF
        `me`'s `I have a direct or indirect pecuniary interest in an agreement with the Public Service of the Commonwealth`
    AND (NOT (    `me`'s `I have that interest only as a member of an incorporated company, in common with its other members`
              AND `me`'s `the number of members of that company` GREATER THAN 25))

-- The answer the Commonwealth Electoral Act baseline asks as a fact ("I am incapable of being chosen under section 44 of the
-- Constitution").
@export Am I incapable of being chosen under section 44 of the Constitution?
GIVEN `me` IS A `My circumstances` @desc Your circumstances
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I incapable of being chosen under section 44` IF
        `Am I disqualified by foreign allegiance` `me`
    OR  `Am I disqualified by a conviction` `me`
    OR  `Am I disqualified as a bankrupt` `me`
    OR  `Am I disqualified by an office or pension` `me`
    OR  `Am I disqualified by an interest in a Commonwealth agreement` `me`

§§ `16, 34 -- Qualifications`

-- s 34: "Until the Parliament otherwise provides, the qualifications of a member of the House of Representatives shall be as
-- follows:-- (i.) He must be of the full age of twenty-one years, and must be an elector entitled to vote at the election of
-- members of the house of Representatives, or a person qualified to become such elector, and must have been for three years at
-- the least a resident within the limits of the Commonwealth as existing at the time when he is chosen: (ii.) He must be a
-- subject of the Queen, either natural-born or for at least five years naturalized under a law of the United Kingdom, or of a
-- Colony which has become or becomes a State, or of the Commonwealth, or of a State."
-- s 16: "The qualifications of a senator shall be the same as those of a member of the House of Representatives."
-- INFERENCE (the text does not say): a person reaches 21 at the start of the 21st anniversary of birth.
@export Do I have the qualifications written in section 34 (and, for a senator, section 16)?
GIVEN `me`      IS A `My circumstances` @desc Your age, electoral status, residence and status as a subject
      `the day` IS A DATE               @desc The day you would be chosen, ISO 8601
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have the section 34 qualifications` IF
        Day `the day` AT LEAST Day (`add years` (`me`'s `my date of birth`) 21)
    AND `me`'s `I am an elector entitled to vote at elections of members of the House of Representatives, or qualified to become one`
    AND `me`'s `years I have been resident within the Commonwealth when I am chosen` AT LEAST 3
    AND (    `me`'s `I am a natural-born subject of the Queen`
         OR  `me`'s `years I have been naturalized under a law of the United Kingdom, a State or colony, or the Commonwealth` AT LEAST 5)

-- s 34 applies only "Until the Parliament otherwise provides". Where the Parliament has provided (the Commonwealth Electoral
-- Act 1918 s 163 does), the qualifications that apply are the Parliament's, asked here as a fact.
@export Do I have the qualifications that apply to me, under section 34 or the law the Parliament has made in its place?
GIVEN `me`      IS A `My circumstances` @desc Your circumstances
      `the day` IS A DATE               @desc The day you would be chosen, ISO 8601
      `the Parliament has otherwise provided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a law of the Parliament now sets the qualifications (the Commonwealth Electoral Act 1918 s 163 does)
      `I have the qualifications the Parliament has provided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether you have them (e.g. age 18, Australian citizen, elector, under s 163)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have the qualifications that apply` IF
    IF `the Parliament has otherwise provided`
    THEN `I have the qualifications the Parliament has provided`
    ELSE `Do I have the section 34 qualifications` `me` `the day`

§§ `43 -- Member of one House ineligible for other`

-- s 43: "A member of either House of the Parliament shall be incapable of being chosen or of sitting as a member of the other
-- House."
@export Am I barred from the House I seek because I sit in the other House (s 43)?
GIVEN `me`    IS A `My circumstances` @desc Whether you already sit in either House
      `house` IS A `House`              @desc The House you want to be chosen for
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 43 bar me` IF
    CONSIDER `house`
    WHEN `the Senate` THEN `me`'s `my seat now` EQUALS `I am a member of the House of Representatives`
    WHEN `the House of Representatives` THEN `me`'s `my seat now` EQUALS `I am a senator`

§ `Am I capable of being chosen`

-- ss 16, 34, 43, 44 together: qualified, and not made incapable by s 43 or s 44.
@export Am I capable of being chosen as a senator or a member of the House of Representatives (ss 16, 34, 43, 44)?
GIVEN `me`      IS A `My circumstances` @desc Your circumstances
      `house`   IS A `House`              @desc The House you want to be chosen for
      `the day` IS A DATE               @desc The day you would be chosen, ISO 8601
      `the Parliament has otherwise provided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a law of the Parliament now sets the qualifications (the Commonwealth Electoral Act 1918 s 163 does)
      `I have the qualifications the Parliament has provided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether you have them
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I capable of being chosen` IF
        `Do I have the qualifications that apply` `me` `the day` `the Parliament has otherwise provided` `I have the qualifications the Parliament has provided`
    AND (NOT `Does section 43 bar me` `me` `house`)
    AND (NOT `Am I incapable of being chosen under section 44` `me`)

§§ `45, 46 -- Once chosen`

-- s 45: "If a senator or member of the House of Representatives-- (i.) Becomes subject to any of the disabilities mentioned in
-- the last preceding section: or (ii.) Takes the benefit, whether by assignment, composition, or otherwise, of any law relating
-- to bankrupt or insolvent debtors: or (iii.) Directly or indirectly takes or agrees to take any fee or honorarium for services
-- rendered to the Commonwealth, or for services rendered in the Parliament to any person or State: his place shall thereupon
-- become vacant."
@export If I am chosen, would my place become vacant (s 45)?
GIVEN `me` IS A `My circumstances` @desc Your circumstances now, as a senator or member
      `I take the benefit of a law relating to bankrupt or insolvent debtors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you take that benefit, by assignment, composition or otherwise
      `I take or agree to take a fee or honorarium for services to the Commonwealth or in the Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you take or agree to take such a fee or honorarium, directly or indirectly
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Would my place become vacant` IF
        `Am I incapable of being chosen under section 44` `me`
    OR  `I take the benefit of a law relating to bankrupt or insolvent debtors`
    OR  `I take or agree to take a fee or honorarium for services to the Commonwealth or in the Parliament`

-- s 46: "Until the Parliament otherwise provides, any person declared by this constitution to be incapable of sitting as a
-- senator or as a member of the House of Representatives shall, for every day on which he so sits, be liable to pay the sum of
-- one hundred pounds to any person who sues for it in any court of competent jurisdiction." Sections 43 and 44 are the ones that
-- declare a person "incapable ... of sitting". Encoded as written: whether the Parliament has otherwise provided is not in this
-- deposit, and the sum is in pounds.
@export What could I be made to pay, in pounds, for sitting while incapable of sitting (s 46, as written)?
GIVEN `me`    IS A `My circumstances` @desc Your circumstances while sitting
      `house` IS A `House`              @desc The House you sit in
      `days`  IS A NUMBER               @desc The number of days on which you sat
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What could I be made to pay for sitting while incapable` IS
    IF `Am I incapable of being chosen under section 44` `me` OR `Does section 43 bar me` `me` `house`
    THEN 100 TIMES `days`
    ELSE 0
